<strong>Scream nails</strong> are back in a big way this Halloween, moving past the generic bats-and-pumpkins roundups into something far more specific: full-on Ghostface energy. If you've scrolled Pinterest or TikTok lately, you've already seen the mask rendered across matte black bases, glossy chrome finishes, and blood-drip French tips. This is the trend everyone's saving to a board right now, worth doing before Halloween passes and your feed moves on. Whether you want one easy accent nail or a full 3D set, there's a version of <strong>scream nails</strong> built for your skill level. This roundup covers 25 ideas across every shape, finish, and commitment level, so you leave knowing exactly which one to try.

## What Are Scream Nails, Exactly?

<strong>Scream nails</strong> are not a vague spooky-season aesthetic. They are a specific, named nail art style built around Ghostface, the masked killer from the *Scream* franchise, and nothing else earns the name. The design centers on recreating the mask's elongated black-and-white face, usually as an accent nail rather than across all ten fingers.

A **Ghostface mask** is the white, screaming, elongated face design worn by the killer in the *Scream* film series, instantly recognisable by its hollow black eyes and open mouth. That silhouette is the entire foundation of the trend. Every variation covered in this roundup, from the simplest stamped accent to a full 3D freehand set, starts from that same shape. What changes is technique, not subject matter. Some artists hand-paint it with a fine liner brush. Others use a stamping plate to get identical results across multiple nails. Either way, the mask itself is non-negotiable. Drop it, and it's just a black-and-white Halloween mani, not a scream nail.

