## Blood-Drip French Tip Scream Nails

Plain black and white is the baseline. **Blood-drip french tip** work is where scream nails start to feel like a genuine sub-style rather than a single accent design, and it's one of the most repeated looks on Etsy listings and Pinterest boards right now.

A blood-drip French tip is a reverse French manicure where the white tip line is replaced with a deep red gradient that trails downward in irregular drips, mimicking a splatter rather than a clean edge. The effect works because it borrows the French tip's built-in structure, meaning it's genuinely easier to execute cleanly than a freehand mask, while still delivering full horror-movie drama. Most nail artists build it with a thin brush, painting the drip shapes freehand in a deep oxblood or true red, then adding one or two darker red dots at the base of each drip for depth.

This variation pairs especially well with a plain black base rather than white, since the red reads more vividly against dark polish. Some versions skip the Ghostface mask entirely and let the blood-drip tip carry the whole design on its own, which makes it a strong option for anyone who wants scream-adjacent nails without committing to a full mask on any nail. Others combine both: mask on one accent nail, blood-drip tips across the rest. That combination has been showing up repeatedly across TikTok tutorials this season and reads as the most complete version of the trend.

