## Black Chrome and Glossy Ghostface Looks

Matte black and white is the classic <strong>scream nails</strong> palette. Black chrome is the finish variation actually trending this season, and it changes the entire mood of the design without touching the mask itself.

**Black chrome scream nails** swap the flat matte base for a mirrored, almost liquid-metal black underneath the Ghostface detailing, applied with a chrome powder buffed over a black gel base before the mask is painted on top. The result catches light in a way flat black never does, giving the whole set a more elevated, less costume-like feel. A high-gloss top coat achieves something similar with less product and less time, simply sealing a standard black base until it reflects like glass rather than absorbing light the way matte finishes do.

Both approaches keep the mask itself unchanged, black and white detailing, same proportions, but the finish underneath shifts the whole design from Halloween-costume energy toward something closer to an actual editorial manicure. This is the version showing up most in the "baddie" and "horror aesthetic" tagged posts rather than strictly Halloween-tagged content, which says something about where this trend is headed beyond October 31st.

