## The Verdict on Scream Nails This Halloween

<strong>Scream nails</strong> are not a trend to sit out this year. The range on offer now, stamped and beginner-friendly on one end, fully sculpted 3D chrome sets on the other, means there's no real excuse for skipping it based on skill level or time. Pick the version that matches what you've actually got: fifteen minutes and a stamping plate, an hour with a liner brush, or a press-on set that arrives ready to apply. Whichever route gets you there, the mask is the whole point, so don't let a generic bats-and-pumpkins mani stand in for the specific, unmistakable look everyone's actually searching for this October. Book it, buy it, or paint it yourself. Just don't let Halloween pass without trying it once.
